        "original_id": "6048a272-3fee-5537-b93b-d6413e1472ed",
        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- People: Caroline Thompson, Tim Burton, Mike Johnson, John August, Pamela Pettler, Carlos Grangel, Henry Selick\n- Films: Edward Scissorhands, The Nightmare Before Christmas, Corpse Bride, James and the Giant Peach\n- Roles: novelist, screenwriter, film director, producer\n- Topics: stop-motion animation, Victorian era setting\n\nFacts:\n- Caroline Thompson was born on April 23, 1956, and she is an American novelist, screenwriter, film director, and producer.\n- Caroline Thompson wrote the screenplays for Tim Burton's films Edward Scissorhands, The Nightmare Before Christmas, and Corpse Bride.\n- Corpse Bride is a 2005 British-American stop-motion-animated musical fantasy film directed by Mike Johnson and Tim Burton.\n- The screenplay for Corpse Bride was written by John August, Caroline Thompson, and Pamela Pettler, based on characters created by Tim Burton and Carlos Grangel.\n- The plot of Corpse Bride is set in a fictional Victorian era village in Europe.\n- Corpse Bride was Tim Burton's third stop-motion feature film as a producer and his first as a director.\n- The previous two Burton-produced stop-motion feature films, The Nightmare Before Christmas and James and the Giant Peach, were directed by Henry Selick.",
        "type": "TextSummary"
      },
